## Carrier owns the complete sensor circuit

- J5.1=3V3_IMU_IN, .2=GND, .3=SDA_3V3, .4=SCL_3V3; matching main J4. U5 IN/EN=3V3_IMU_IN; C5 input, C6 output. Both >=1uF effective after bias; selected 4.7uF 0603. U5 OUT=1V8_IMU, never a host connector pin.
- U2 ICM-20948: **8 VDDIO and 13 VDD to 1V8_IMU**, each with its own 100n C8/C7; 10 REGOUT to C9 100n to GND only; 18 and **20 RESV to GND**; 19 RESV NC. Pins1–6,14–17 NC. 11 FSYNC=GND; 9 AD0=GND (address 0x68); 22 nCS=1V8_IMU; 23=SCL_1V8, 24=SDA_1V8. 7 AUX_CL,21 AUX_DA NC; 12 INT NC because polling is intentional. No invented exposed pad or 3.3V strap. Existing DS-000189 pin table/typical circuit applies. [source](https://jlcpcb.com/api/file/downloadByFileSystemAccessId/8588885225937625088)
- U3 PCA9306DCUR: 1=GND, 2=VREF1/1V8_IMU, 3=SCL_1V8, 4=SDA_1V8, 5=SDA_3V3, 6=SCL_3V3, **7 VREF2 joined 8 EN**, R20 200k from that joined node to 3V3_IMU_IN. This is the TI reference-bias topology, not a conventional directly supplied VCC pin. R16/R17 4.7k low-domain pulls; R18/R19 4.7k high-domain pulls. [source](https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/pca9306.pdf)
- Host pins remain open-drain; main internal pulls disabled. VDD/VDDIO are 1.8V together, eliminating independent rail sequencing assumptions. Verify startup/rundown, stuck-bus recovery and no ICM pin exceeding its 1.95V-domain limits. A 1.8V regulator alone would **not** make direct ESP wiring safe.
- Start I2C at **100kHz**, FIFO polling every 5–10ms; target 200Hz accel/gyro and 50Hz mag subject to measured bus/FIFO latency. Read/configure the internal magnetometer correctly via the ICM's documented internal-master/bypass mechanism; do not assume accel/gyro WHO_AM_I establishes nine-axis operation. Validate identities/data-ready/overflow, alignment and calibration. No suspend/wake-by-INT feature is promised.
- **400kHz is conditional** on measured rise <=300ns and bus capacitance budget. With 4.7k, 0.8473*R*C gives about 75pF maximum per domain before tolerance/margin; target <=60pF, including connector/cable/pins/probes. At 100kHz target <=200pF. Check low-level sink current with both-domain pull-ups, not one side alone. Never add duplicate pull-ups or extend the cable arbitrarily.

